  data: {
    LLM: "Save your high cards (13, 14, 15) for high-value Mice (+8, +9, +10). Use your low cards (1, 2) to avoid taking Vultures.\n\nThe 'Cancellation' rule is key. If you think your opponent will play a 15 for a +10 mouse, playing a 15 yourself cancels both, letting a player who played a 1 win the high-value card.\n\nLevel-k thinking: 'I know they think I'll play a 15, so they will play a 15 to cancel me, so I'll play a 14 to win when their 15s are gone.'",
    Player: "Save your high cards (13, 14, 15) for high-value Mice (+8, +9, +10). Use your low cards (1, 2) to avoid taking Vultures.\n\nThe 'Cancellation' rule is key. If you think your opponent will play a 15 for a +10 mouse, playing a 15 yourself cancels both, letting a player who played a 1 win the high-value card.\n\nLevel-k thinking: 'I know they think I'll play a 15, so they will play a 15 to cancel me, so I'll play a 14 to win when their 15s are gone.'",
